The copied format implementations retain their original MIT license and NOTICE
files under `format-notices/<format>/`. Those notices include third-party
dependency and behavioral-reference attribution, including meshoptimizer,
yaml, and black-reader-js.

The bundled Black definition JSON is a generated CarbonEngineJS schema artifact
copied from `format-carbon` revision
`d2a3c67cf3d46e8ba78ca19e66558d868178ec24`. Its exact digest and retention
purpose are recorded in `docs/formats/provenance.md`; no CarbonEngine source file or
game asset is embedded in that generated definition snapshot.

The GR2/GSF implementation is included under `formats/gr2`, migrated from
`format-gr2` after its former EUPL-derived BitKnit2 decoder was replaced by a
validated clean-room implementation and the package was relicensed MIT. Its
retained license, provenance, and third-party notices live under
`format-notices/gr2/` and `docs/formats/provenance.md`.

The modern cFSD decoder and reviewed dataset schemas are included under
`formats/fsd/64`, migrated from the MIT-licensed `tools-fsd` donor package.
They decode caller-supplied bytes and include no acquired game data, decoded
tables, or native loader modules. The retained donor notice and license live
under `format-notices/fsd/`.
